━━━ What makes a GOOD root node ━━━
A good root encodes at least two of:
  (a) Anatomical localisation  — where the lesion likely resides (cortex / cord /
      plexus / root / peripheral nerve / vascular / systemic / visceral mass …)
  (b) Mechanism category       — compressive, infiltrative, demyelinating, ischaemic,
      inflammatory, metabolic, toxic, neoplastic …
  (c) Temporal pattern         — acute onset (<24 h), subacute (days–weeks),
      chronic-progressive (months–years)
  (d) Alarming systemic context — constitutional features (weight loss, night sweats),
      risk-factor cluster, high-danger urgency tier

Good examples:
  ✓ "Subacute Progressive Unilateral Upper-Limb Motor-Sensory Deficit with
     Constitutional Alarm Signs"
  ✓ "Acute Anterior Circulation Ischaemic Stroke Syndrome"
  ✓ "Subacute Compressive Brachial Plexopathy Syndrome"
  ✓ "Acute Decompensated Heart Failure Syndrome"
  ✓ "Subacute Bilateral Lower-Limb Weakness with Bladder Dysfunction (Cord Level)"

━━━ What is FORBIDDEN ━━━
  ✗ Paraphrasing the chief complaint: "Acute Right Arm Weakness Syndrome"
  ✗ Single-symptom labels:            "Right Arm Weakness"
  ✗ Premature diagnosis:              "Pancoast Tumour Syndrome"
  ✗ Vague filler:                     "Neurological Syndrome"

━━━ Algorithm ━━━
1. Enumerate ALL key findings (not just the chief complaint):
   motor/sensory deficits, constitutional features, risk factors,
   vital-sign abnormalities, exam asymmetries, time course.
2. Ask: which anatomical compartment and mechanism best unifies these findings?
3. Note any systemic alarm features that raise urgency or suggest a specific
   mechanism (e.g., weight loss + heavy smoking → suspect neoplasm).
4. Compose a root label from: [temporal pattern] + [anatomical localisation] +
   [mechanism hint if strong] + [alarm-feature qualifier if present].
5. If the root node already exists and new evidence contradicts it, set
   need_root_revision: true.

━━━ Constraints ━━━
- Do NOT use an isolated lab value or single vital sign as the root.
- External knowledge retrieval is permitted only if the case frame is genuinely
  rare or specialty-specific and you cannot form a coherent root without it.

